// Prototype power resources are cloned from existing spell resources.
// The table remains authoritative for level, discipline and pool cost.

// Saving-throw difficulty shared by every generated power.
//
// D&D 3.5 sets a power's save DC at 10 + power level + key ability modifier.
// The Infinity Engine has no DC: a target saves when its own d20 roll plus the
// effect's savebonus meets the save target from its class and level. Only the
// relative part of the tabletop formula survives that translation, so each
// level module defines psion_levelN_save_penalty carrying a power-level term
// of -(N - 1). Level 1 therefore sits at the baseline and each higher tier is
// one point harder to resist, preserving the spread the tabletop formula
// produces without inflating Psion powers against ordinary BG spells.
//
// The key-ability half cannot scale with the manifester. GemRB's Python API
// exposes no way to vary an installed SPL's savebonus by the caster's runtime
// stats: ModifyEffect only moves an effect's target coordinates, and the only
// substitution hook, PrepareSpontaneousCast, would require a separate SPL per
// Intelligence bracket for all sixty-one powers. Chargen enforces Intelligence
// 15 (see class-common.tpa), so every Psion has at least a +2 key-ability
// modifier; that guaranteed share is baked in here, and Intelligence above 15
// does not further improve save difficulty.
//
// This constant is the one place the translation trades fidelity for
// tractability, and it is balance-affecting: setting it to 0 reverts every
// power to the engine's default save difficulty.
OUTER_SET psion_key_ability_save_penalty = (0 - 2)

// Augmentation ceiling.
//
// D&D 3.5 caps a single manifestation at the manifester's level in power
// points, and the Psion table runs to level 20, so an augment ladder should
// reach 20 PP rather than stopping at the highest base cost. The runtime
// already refuses tiers above the actor's level (Psionics.py), so a long ladder
// costs nothing at low level beyond the generated resources themselves.
//
// This must match MAX_AUGMENT_COST in psion/tools/generate_augment_tables.py,
// which produces PSIONAUGMENT.2DA and the per-parent selector tables from the
// same number. validate_core.py asserts the two agree. Lowering it here and
// rerunning the generator is the supported way to shrink the ladders.
OUTER_SET psion_max_augment_cost = 20
